usage: check.py [-h] [--run RUN] [--publish] [--plan] [--timeout TIMEOUT]

Cold-check the symbolic arbitrary-horizon PID measurement proof. The checker
compiles immutable snapshots of the complete imported local source closure,
instantiates every canonical goal with its claimed theorem, prints the actual
inherited assumptions, and independently checks both proof and goal-
certificate modules. --publish installs current hash-bound receipts; ordinary
replay preserves all published evidence. --run charges commands to an
existing, open proof-author session; otherwise reproduction is tool-only.

options:
  -h, --help         show this help message and exit
  --run RUN          existing open metered proof-author run
  --publish          install current canonical receipts
  --plan             dependency plan only; no proof acceptance
  --timeout TIMEOUT
